1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:08,458
The brush clears a small stone shrine with a tall top. Before the Gupta age there were no free-standing stone temples in India.

2
00:00:08,458 --> 00:00:15,156
Then they appeared, first simple and flat, then taller. When did a temple first get a tower?

3
00:00:34,317 --> 00:00:44,076
How do we know? The temples themselves survive. Archaeologists dug up shrines at Sanchi, Tigawa, Bhitargaon and Deogarh.

4
00:00:44,076 --> 00:00:48,041
Inscriptions name donors and kings who paid for them.

5
00:01:05,683 --> 00:01:08,108
Early Gupta temples are small.

6
00:01:08,108 --> 00:01:14,462
The Temple at Sanchi, Temple Seventeen, has a flat roof and a square sanctum, called the garbhagriha.

7
00:01:14,462 --> 00:01:20,853
A small pillared porch is in front. At Tigawa and Bhitargaon, later temples grew higher.

8
00:01:20,853 --> 00:01:26,433
The Bhitargaon temple is built of brick and has a high tower, and carved terracotta panels.

9
00:01:26,433 --> 00:01:32,731
The Deogarh temple, in Uttar Pradesh, has the earliest surviving shikhara, or tower, in stone.

10
00:01:32,731 --> 00:01:36,497
In the Deccan, the caves of Ajanta were carved and painted.

11
00:01:36,497 --> 00:01:44,908
Ajanta paintings show scenes from the Jataka tales, stories of the Buddha's earlier lives. Metalwork was also fine.

12
00:01:44,908 --> 00:01:51,985
The Delhi iron pillar and a copper Buddha image from Sultanganj, over two metres tall, show metal skill.

13
00:01:51,985 --> 00:01:57,311
Gupta sculpture is known for its calm and balance, as in the Sarnath images.

14
00:02:14,950 --> 00:02:22,294
Old name, new name. The inner shrine of a temple is called the garbhagriha, which means the womb chamber.

15
00:02:22,294 --> 00:02:27,503
In English it is called the sanctum. It is the heart of every Hindu temple.

16
00:02:45,150 --> 00:02:55,963
Carve this tip into memory. Flat, brick, stone, tower:. Sanchi, Bhitargaon, Deogarh. Three sites in order of growth.

17
00:02:55,963 --> 00:02:58,968
You have a story of how the temple grew.

18
00:03:16,617 --> 00:03:32,908
Dig Quiz. Pause and name it. Number one. What is the inner shrine of a temple called? The answer: the garbhagriha. Number two.

19
00:03:32,908 --> 00:03:50,148
Which caves are famous for Jataka paintings? The answer: Ajanta. Number three. Which Delhi monument shows Gupta metal skill?

20
00:03:50,148 --> 00:04:00,159
The answer: the Mehrauli iron pillar. Now one line for Mains. Trace the evolution of the temple in the Gupta period.

21
00:04:21,817 --> 00:04:29,260
The temple goes into its case. It is a small model of a great step in building. Three facts to take away.

22
00:04:29,260 --> 00:04:36,571
A model of an early Gupta temple. Sanctum and a pillared porch. The shikhara first appears in stone.

23
00:04:36,571 --> 00:04:40,234
Next gallery: The Guptas Fade.

